389-392	156,667,1284,1605 - 603,1335,772,1605 - 603,1295,745,1335 - 1133,1425,1284,1605	389 Small-flowered Honeysuckle. 392. Flowers, &c. of Fly-Honeysuckle, No. 11.	On the right (389), a Small-flowered Honeysuckle stem with pairs of joined leaves and a crowded cluster of small two-lipped flowers at the top; on the left (392), a Fly-Honeysuckle twig bearing a pair of hairy flowers on one stalk, with a long leaf.
390	603,1295,770,1586	390. A separate flower.	A single two-lipped honeysuckle flower on its small round ovary, with the stamens and style standing out of the open throat.
391	1135,1429,1260,1594	391. An ovary divided lengthwise, and magnified.	An ovary split lengthwise and magnified, showing two cells side by side, each holding hanging ovules.
